Subject: [PATCH] iommu/qcom: Treat v1 secure contexts as secured

The v1 secure context (qcom,msm-iommu-v1-sec) was not marked
secured_ctx, so probe resumed its parent and read/wrote ARM_SMMU_CB_FSR
on the secure bank. On angler's GPU SMMU that reset the SoC immediately
after the secure page table was initialized: the trace stopped between
"parent resume returned 0" and "FSR cleared" for iommu-ctx@a000.

Mark v1 secure contexts secured like the v2 ones, so the non-secure
driver leaves the bank to the secure world. The compatible is already
used to decide whether a secure page table is needed.

Apply with git apply after 0035 for the bring-up image; 0035 is
diagnostic logging, this one is the functional fix.

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -927,7 +927,8 @@
 		return irq;
 	dev_info(dev, "iommu ctx: mapped, irq %d\n", irq);
 
-	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,msm-iommu-v2-sec"))
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,msm-iommu-v1-sec") ||
+	    of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "qcom,msm-iommu-v2-sec"))
 		ctx->secured_ctx = true;
 
 	/* clear IRQs before registering fault handler, just in case the
